1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,780
What would happen to your body if
you fell into the Mariana Trench?

2
00:00:04,883 --> 00:00:07,293
You drop into the western Pacific Ocean,

3
00:00:07,763 --> 00:00:11,653
directly above a depth of 10,935 metres.

4
00:00:12,028 --> 00:00:15,758
Cold water triggers cold shock
and uncontrolled gasping,

5
00:00:15,908 --> 00:00:17,638
which can kill within 2 minutes.

6
00:00:18,717 --> 00:00:19,787
With your mouth submerged,

7
00:00:20,377 --> 00:00:22,947
gasping forces water
in and causes drowning.

8
00:00:23,372 --> 00:00:24,862
As your body sinks deeper,

9
00:00:25,032 --> 00:00:29,362
rising hydrostatic pressure
shrinks flexible gas-filled spaces.

10
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:34,970
This difference in pressure causes
injuries to gas-containing internal organs

11
00:00:34,970 --> 00:00:37,020
like your lungs and ears.

12
00:00:38,183 --> 00:00:41,433
In short, cold shock and
drowning can kill you in minutes.

13
00:00:41,753 --> 00:00:42,643
As you descend,

14
00:00:42,973 --> 00:00:47,203
rising water pressure can injure
your gas-containing internal organs.

15
00:00:48,350 --> 00:00:51,060
Would you ever dare to
explore the ocean deeps?

